<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Amplitude and period from an equation</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>For the wave \(y = {@wdisp@}\), where \(x\) is in degrees, find</p><div>(a) the amplitude [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) the period [[input:ans2]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) The amplitude is how far the wave rises above its mean line: the size of \({@ad@}\), which is \({@ampd@}\).[[if test="is(a < 0)"]] The minus sign turns the wave upside down but does not change its height.[[/if]]</p><p>(b) The period is how far along the axis before the wave repeats itself: \(360^\circ \div {@b@} = {@per@}^\circ\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: period and amplitude of a sin bx, including negative a and fractional b. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 2, Chapter 7, Section B, B2 and B5. */
L: [[1,3,2],[0,-2,3],[1,5,1/2],[0,4,4],[1,-3,3/2],[0,5/2,6],[1,6,1/3],[0,-5,2/3],[1,-3/2,5],[0,2,3/4]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
fs: L[ix][1]; a: L[ix][2]; b: L[ix][3];
nice(v) := block([r], r: floor(1000*v+1/2)/1000, if integerp(r) then r else float(r));
fname: if fs = 1 then "\\sin" else "\\cos";
ad: if integerp(a) then string(a) else string(float(a));
bx: if b = 1 then " x" elseif integerp(b) then sconcat(" ", string(b), "x") elseif num(b) = 1 then sconcat("\\tfrac{x}{", string(denom(b)), "}") else sconcat("\\tfrac{", string(num(b)), "x}{", string(denom(b)), "}");
wdisp: sconcat(ad, fname, bx);
amp: abs(a); per: 360/b; ampd: if integerp(amp) then amp else float(amp);
namp: -amp; damp: 2*amp; mper: 360*b; bper: b; hper: 180/b;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, a={@a@}, b={@b@}, amplitude {@amp@}, period {@per@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Trigonometry III: amplitude and period from an equation</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.5: Find the amplitude and period of y = a sin bx or y = a cos bx, including negative a and fractional b.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from B2 and B5 in Section B of Chapter 7 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 2 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: new functions with negative and fractional coefficients, randomised over a curated list, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
